.TH SLML 1 "2026-10-26" "slml 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slml \- native browser and tools for the Strict Layout Markup Language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slml
.I file.slml-or-folder
.br
.B slml view
.I file.slml-or-folder
.br
.B slml check
.IR file-or-folder ...
.br
.B slml serve
.RI [ folder ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-open ]
.RB [ \-\-web | \-\-html ]
.br
.B slml build
.IR file-or-folder ...
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.br
.B slml render
.I file.slml
.RB [ \-o
.IR out.png ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slml
opens original SLML documents in its own native browser. It parses, validates,
lays out and paints the source directly with its Rust renderer and bundled
fonts. A folder opens its
.I index.slml
and becomes the site root for imports and absolute paths.
.PP
The native browser follows local links and anchors, scrolls, keeps navigation
history and reloads when a page, import or image changes. It does not generate
HTML or launch a system web browser to display the document. Close its window
to exit.
.PP
HTML export and web-hosted viewers are optional compatibility tools selected
explicitly. Native form editing, text selection and remote HTTP(S) document
loading remain planned.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B view
Open a file or site folder in the native browser. This is the default action.
A build without the
.I viewer
feature reports an error instead of opening another browser.
.TP
.B check
Report errors without opening a window or writing output. Folders are checked
recursively. Invalid documents and broken local links produce diagnostics.
.TP
.B serve
Serve original SLML files and assets on 127.0.0.1 (port 4000 or the next free
one). The root URL returns index.slml as text/slml. With --open, run the native
browser against the local site; closing its window stops this command.
Use --web to explicitly select the web-hosted WebAssembly viewer, or --html
for an HTML export preview. Only those explicit adapters open a system web
browser when combined with --open. Without --open, stop with Ctrl+C.
.TP
.B build
Explicitly export HTML. A file writes page.html and shared styles/fonts in
_slml/. A folder exports pages and assets into folder/_site (or -o output).
Libraries of styles and components are skipped. Invalid pages and broken
links are reported instead of writing guessed output.
.TP
.B render
Render a page to a PNG image with the native renderer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIpath\fR
Explicit export file or folder. A .png output uses the native image renderer;
other output paths select the HTML compatibility exporter. Without an output
path or export command, the document opens in SLML.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " folder"
Site root for paths starting with /. A folder input is its own root. For a
file input, default to the current folder if it contains the file, otherwise
the file's folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " px"
Page width for PNG output (default 900).
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " n"
Pixel density for PNG output and the native browser (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
First port to try for serve (default 4000).
.TP
.B \-\-open
With serve, open the native SLML browser. With --web or --html, open the
explicitly selected web adapter instead.
.TP
.B \-\-web
With serve, explicitly use the optional WebAssembly viewer in a web browser.
Requires make web followed by rebuilding slml.
.TP
.B \-\-html
Explicitly select HTML export, or the HTML server preview with serve.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only errors.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the program and language version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if checking, export or opening the browser fails. Invalid
pages in the interactive browser appear as SLML error pages.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
slml examples/starter/
slml handbook/
slml view index.slml
slml serve my-site/ \-\-open
slml check my-site/
slml render index.slml \-o preview.png
slml build my-site/ \-o public/
slml serve my-site/ \-\-web \-\-open
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The SLML handbook (handbook/ or docs/handbook/ in the source repository),
SPEC.md and ROADMAP.md.
